  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Stripe owns state",
      "items": [
        "The table is a projection; username holds the Stripe customer id",
        "NewUser and StripeSync re-fetch the subscription from the Stripe API, so repeated or out-of-order events are harmless",
        "An ended subscription never overwrites a newer one for the same customer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Three endpoints, built",
      "items": [
        "Each Lambda has its own HTTP API (20 req/s) and least-privilege IAM role",
        "Stripe sends subscription.created to NewUser; updates, deletes and customer.updated to StripeSync",
        "Code in newsletter/, pushed with newsletter/deploy.sh"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Unsubscribe",
      "items": [
        "Letter link opens the hidden unsubscribe.html with ?c=<customer id>&t=<HMAC token>",
        "Reader types their email; the page POSTs {c, t, email}. UnsubscribeUser checks the token, then the email against the DynamoDB row",
        "Then cancels at period end in Stripe (metadata email_opt_out) and re-syncs the row: receives_letters false at once",
        "The mail header's one-click POST needs the token only; there is no GET route"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Secrets in SSM (us-east-2)",
      "items": [
        "Two webhook signing secrets, a restricted Stripe key, the unsubscribe HMAC key",
        "Each Lambda can read only the parameters it uses",
        "Nothing secret in the repo or config.js"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Planned, not built",
      "items": [
        "S3 issues bucket, send-issue Lambda, welcome and goodbye emails",
        "SES is in the sandbox and needs a custom sending domain"
      ]
    }
  ]
